  "term": "Neurolinguistic Programming",
  "definition": "Neurolinguistic programming is an approach that uses models of how communication and subjective experience influence each other. It focuses on patterns linking the brain, language, and body, and uses these patterns to try to alter a person’s internal representations and behavior.",
